---
description: Never attribute Git commits to Cursor as author or co-author
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Cursor co-author

- Never mention Cursor as a commit author or co-author.
- Never add this trailer (or any variant) to commit messages:

```
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

- Also forbid: `Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, or any other AI/Cursor attribution line.
- If a tool or hook injects Cursor co-author text, remove it before finishing the commit.
- Preserve only human authorship configured by the repository owner.
